-- title:
--   Mod p q-expansion field of X_H(M) lies in that of X_{H'}(M/p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M \ge 1$ an integer with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup, and assume that every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ whose image under the reduction map $\mathrm{ZMod.unitsMap} : (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial already lies in $H$. Let $K$ be a field of characteristic $p$. For a subgroup $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) $\Gamma$ is the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by the set of quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_g$, where $f$ and $g$ run over modular forms of one and the same weight $k$ on the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ admitting integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ (in the sense of `IsIntegralQExp`) with the reduction of $p_g$ nonzero in $K((q))$. Here [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) denotes the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ consisting of the matrices of $\Gamma_0(M)$ whose lower right entry reduces modulo $M$ into $H$, and [`ModularCurve.infSubgroup p M H hpM`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L246) is the image $H'$ of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. The assertion is the inclusion of intermediate fields $\bar F_{\Gamma_H(M)} \le \bar F_{\Gamma_{H'}(M/p)}$ inside $K((q))$.
--
--   Under the hypothesis on $H$ one has $\Gamma_H(M) = \Gamma_{H'}(M/p) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$, so the reverse inclusion is formal and the two fields coincide: in characteristic $p$ the $q$-expansion function field at level $M$ collapses onto the one at level $M/p$, which in characteristic zero it extends with degree $p+1$. This is the function-field shadow of the Deligne–Rapoport description of the special fibre at $p \,\|\, M$, whose component through the cusp $\infty$ maps isomorphically to $X_{H'}(M/p)$; it is used in the identifications of full-level modular function fields and the attendant separability statements for $p = 2$ and $p = 3$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_le_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_infSubgroup.lean

